      "definition": "The inverse trigonometric functions are called arcsine, arccosine, and arctangent (also represented as sin⁻¹x, cos⁻¹x, and tan⁻¹x). Because the corresponding trigonometric functions are periodic, they are only invertible if they have restricted domains.",
      "aliases": [
        "inverse cosine"
      ],
      "sourceLabel": "CED 3.9.A.2"
    },
    {
